			<h2>Associate Professor of Mathematics</h2>
			<p>Welcome to my homepage. I am an Associate Professor at the  <a href="http://www.math.uiuc.edu" target="_top"> University of Illinois at Urbana-Champaign</a>.</p> 

			<h2>Research Interests</h2>
			<p> My research lies in the field of Probability Theory and its interactions with models of Statistical Physics. In particular I am interested in First and Last passage percolation, Random growth models, Stein's method, Concentration inequalities, Spin glasses, Random Graphs and Random Matrices.</p>
			
			<h2>About Me</h2>
			<p>I obtained my Ph.D. in <a href="http://www.stat.berkeley.edu">Statistics</a> from <a href="http://www.berkeley.edu">UC Berkeley</a> under the supervision of <a href="http://statweb.stanford.edu/~souravc/">Sourav Chatterjee</a> and <a href="http://www.stat.berkeley.edu/~evans">Steve Evans</a>.<br>
				I was a Courant Instructor and Simons Fellow in the <a href="http://www.math.nyu.edu">Department of Mathematics</a> at the <a href="http://www.cims.nyu.edu"> Courant Institute of Mathematical Sciences, NYU</a>  and a Harrison Early-career Assistant Professor in the <a href="http://www2.warwick.ac.uk/fac/sci/statistics/">Department of Statistics</a> at the <a href="http://www2.warwick.ac.uk">University of Warwick</a>.
				Before that, I did my undergraduate and masters study from <a href= "http://www.isical.ac.in">Indian Statistical Institute, Kolkata</a> with specialization in Mathematical Statistics and Probability.
			</p>
			
